{"name":"Rob Roy","hex":"#ddad56","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Rob Roy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cocktail made with Scotch whisky, vermouth and bitters."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A locality in the Inverell council area, north eastern New South Wales, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Rob_Roy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Christmas Hills, Victoria","blocks":[{"text":"Christmas Hills is a locality in Victoria, Australia, 35 km (22 mi) north-east of Melbourne's Central Business District, located within the Shire of Nillumbik local government area. Christmas Hills recorded a population of 365 at the 2021 census."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christmas_Hills%2C_Victoria"},{"title":"Banks, Australian Capital Territory","blocks":[{"text":"Banks is a suburb in the Canberra, Australia district of Tuggeranong. It is the most southerly suburb of Canberra. The suburb is named after Sir Joseph Banks (1743–1820), the botanist who accompanied Captain James Cook to Botany Bay in 1770. The suburb was gazetted on 12 March 1987. The theme of the street names is botany or natural history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Shops_in_Banks%2C_Australian_Capital_Territory.jpg/330px-Shops_in_Banks%2C_Australian_Capital_Territory.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banks%2C_Australian_Capital_Territory"},{"title":"Rob Roy (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Rob Roy is an 1817 historical novel by Walter Scott, one of the Waverley novels. It is probably set in 1715, the year of the first Jacobite rising, and the social and economic background to that event are an important element in the novel, though it is not treated directly. The depiction of Rob Roy bears little relation to the historical figure: \"there are two Rob Roys. One lived and breathed. The other is a good story, a lively tale set in the past. Both may be accepted as ‘valid', but they serve different needs and interests.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Rob_Roy_title_page.jpg/330px-Rob_Roy_title_page.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rob_Roy_(novel)"},{"title":"Roy","blocks":[{"text":"Roy is both a given name and a family surname with varied origins."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roy"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Sugarloaf_Reservoir.jpg/500px-Sugarloaf_Reservoir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Sugarloaf_Reservoir.jpg/1280px-Sugarloaf_Reservoir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Sugarloaf_Reservoir.jpg/500px-Sugarloaf_Reservoir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASugarloaf_Reservoir.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/LanyonStationAerialView1950.jpg/330px-LanyonStationAerialView1950.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/LanyonStationAerialView1950.jpg/330px-LanyonStationAerialView1950.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial view of Lanyon Station, 1950","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALanyonStationAerialView1950.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Banks_panorama.jpg/500px-Banks_panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Banks_panorama.jpg/1280px-Banks_panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org